les:
Comme l'amour, comme la mort;
Et j'ai fait les plus belles de belle argile
Sèche et fragile.

lesson:
With stories to jabber, and stones to throw;
He'll fetch you a lesson that costs you sore--
Scratch a lover, and find a foe.

lesser:
That hardly stirs in manhood's breast;
And as the sun feeds lesser lights,
As planets have their satellites,

lesbia:
'Tis with the heart of Lilith that I swear,
'Tis with the love of Lesbia and Lucrece;
And thus as well my love must lose some part

Death devours all lovely things;
Lesbia with her sparrow
Shares the darkness,--presently
